# Title flythrough: attract demo frames ~607-1086, camera 29 (cam\cp_title.bin), stage 1 courtyard.
# Derived from game\scene_capture.txt (HOTD2_SCENECAP=1) - which models the original drew and how they
# were placed relative to the camera (notes/progress.md, Milestone 8). Not yet loaded from the game's own
# stage/event tables.
#
# camera <id>                       camera path (time = frames since the camera started)
# static <modelId>                  drawn at identity world (confirmed: 100% of single-camera frames)
# sky <modelId> [scale S] [yaw A0] [yaw_per_frame R]
#                                   translated to the camera position every frame (confirmed); the optional
#                                   rotation/scale of model 6048 is FITTED from the capture (hypothesis:
#                                   ~4 engine angle units per frame), not traced in code.
camera 29
static 6139
static 6091
static 6093
# Environment: defaults (no env ops run during the title). Captured: light direction (0,0,1) world = env angles 0, 0
# (639 states), AMBIENT 0xB2B2B2 / diffuse 0.98 / ambient 0.3, fog start 131070 (none). See game::Environment.
env default
# 2D: Title_DrawLogo 0x004960A0 and PRESS START 0x004067D0 (both traced). Blink phase TRACED: the counter 0x005A4D44 equals the
# boot frame counter 0x009A5C40 (HUD_Init 0x004066D0 runs once at boot), which is capture frame + 1 when the HUD draws.
overlay title
overlay press_start phase 1
# Sky: Sky_Task 0x004132D0 type 0 (12/frame). Sky_Create 0x004134D0 leaves the yaw uninitialised, so the title starts from
# leftover memory; 180687068 at frame 608 reproduces the 479 captured title frames (HYPOTHESIS, notes/agents/effects.md).
# The large value makes the float angle conversion snap to 1/512-rad steps, like the original.
sky_task 0 608 180687068
